   "args": {
    "summary": "Model built and all L1/L2/L3 checks passed.\n\nRoot cause of the earlier failure: support.3.dofs (Abutment 3) was accepted with longitudinal=\"spring\". Abutment 3 carries PTFE sliding laminated elastomeric bearings (instance bearing:3 has sliding=true), and governing rule MR-03 requires a PTFE sliding bearing to be longitudinally free (Kh=0), vertical spring, rotation free. Setting it to \"spring\" created a spurious second longitudinal restraint (besides fixed Pier 1), over-restraining the 3-span continuous girder. The decision was revised to {vertical: spring, longitudinal: free, rotation: free}, consistent with supports 0 and 2, and generate_model then succeeded.\n\nModel summary:\n- Three-span continuous unit, 20 + 25 + 20 m; structure.system = continuous (spine_beam_2d); precast small-box girders, 4 per span, C50, self-weight only.\n- Supports: A0/A3/A2 (Abutment 0, Pier 2, Abutment 3) PTFE sliding (longitudinal free, Kh=0); A1 (Pier 1) plain laminated elastomeric, longitudinally fixed (Kh = 26250 kN/m). All vertical spring Kv ≈ 11.33e6 kN/m, rotations free.\n- Lane: 3 lanes, one-way, Class I, qk = 10.5 kPa, xi = 0.78, Pk = 300/310/300 kN; impact factor mu = 0.288 from f1 = 5.573 Hz (JTGD60-4.3.2).\n\nResults: first three vertical frequencies 5.573 / 8.426 / 10.186 Hz. Self-weight reactions at support lines 820.5, 2764.1, 2764.1, 820.5 kN; midspan moments 2690/2968/2690 kNm; support moments -5649/-5649 kNm. Lane-load max positive moment 5341.5 kNm, max negative moment -3864.0 kNm."
   },
